{title: 548 - Now Praise the Hidden God of Love}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #548 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 548}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Now [F]praise [Edim]the [Dm]hidden [C7]God of love
[F/A]In [Bb]whom [C7/G]we [F/A]all [G/B]must [C]live [Gm]and [C]move,
[C]Who [F]shepherds [Dm]us, [Gm]at every [C7]stage
[F/A]Thro' [Bb]youth, [C7/G]maturity, [F/C]and [C7]age.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Who [F]challenged [Gm]us, when [C7]were young
[F/A]To [Bb]storm [C7/G]the [F/A]citadels [Gm]of [C]wrong;
[C]In [F]care [Am]for [Dm]others [C7]taught us how
[F/A]God's [Bb]true [C7/G]community [F/C]must [C7]grow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Who [F]bids [Edim]us [Dm]never [C7]lose our zest,
[F/A]Tho' [Bb]age [C7/G]is [F/A]urging [C]us [Gm]to [C]rest,
[C]But [F]proves [Dm]to [Gm]us that [C7]we have still
[F/A]A [Bb]work [C7/G]to [F/A]do, [Bb]a place [F/C]to [C7]fill.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Then [F]talk [Edim]no [Dm]more [Gm]of [C7]wasted time,
[F/A]But [Bb]Godward [F/A]look, [G/B]and [C]upward climb,
[C]Content [Am]to [Dm]sleep, [Gm]when [C7]day is done,
[F/A]And [Bb]rise [C7/G]refreshed, [Bb]and travel [C7]on.
{end_of_verse}
